<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">879–933</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Kingdom of Provence, Cisjurane Burgundy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, or the Kingdom of Provence, was the kingdom founded in 879 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence">Boso of Vienne</a> was elected king at Mantaille, covering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley and Provence. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-blind">Louis the Blind</a> was crowned emperor in 901 but blinded in 905, and real power passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles">Hugh of Arles</a>. Around 933 its rights passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-of-burgundy">Rudolf II of Upper Burgundy</a>, uniting the two kingdoms into what became the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-burgundy.jpg" alt="Lower Burgundy" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Hoch_und_Niederburgund_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
